@startuml
' Figure - Communication Diagram: risk assessment collaboration
!include _header.txt
hide empty members
top to bottom direction

object ": Route"                     as RT
object "scorer : EvidenceRiskScorer" as SC
object "ev : EvidenceItem"           as EV
object ": CustodyLog [*]"            as CL
object ": WeightProvider"            as WP
object ": InteractionRules"          as IR
object "report : RiskReport"         as RP

RT --> SC : "1: score(ev)"
SC --> EV : "2: read indicators"
SC --> CL : "3: read handling history"
SC --> SC : "4: normalise each indicator"
SC --> WP : "5: currentWeights()"
SC --> SC : "6: base := sum(w * n)"
SC --> IR : "7: fired(indicators)"
IR --> SC : "8: effects"
SC --> SC : "9: bonus := min(sum, 0.30)"
SC --> SC : "10: classify(base + bonus)"
SC --> RP : "11: create"
RP --> RT : "12: factors, reasons"

note top of SC
  The same interaction a sequence diagram
  would show, organised by STRUCTURE
  rather than by time: the emphasis falls
  on which objects collaborate, and the
  numbering carries the ordering.
end note

note bottom of IR
  Step 9 applies the cap. Without it,
  several rules firing together would
  saturate every item and destroy the
  ranking the feature exists to provide.
end note
@enduml
